  "question": {
    "text": "If the tangent to the parabola <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></math> at a point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> is also a tangent to the ellipse, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> then <math><mi>&#945;</mi></math> is equal to:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Since <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> lies on the parabola <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>&#946;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mi>&#946;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Tangent to a parabola&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></math> at a point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Therefore, tangent to the parabola <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>&#946;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>&#8901;</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>&#946;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#946;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>&#946;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mi>i</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>Tangent to parabola is also a tangent to ellipse</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mfenced></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>And, a line&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></math>&nbsp;is a tangent to the ellipse&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;if&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p>Using the condition <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>&#946;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#946;</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>&#946;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>&#946;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>&#946;</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>&#946;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Using Sridharacharya&#39;s Formula&nbsp;the roots of a quadratic equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>&#177;</mo><msqrt><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>c</mi></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>&#946;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#177;</mo><msqrt><msup><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>&#946;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#177;</mo><msqrt><mn>8</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>&#946;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>&#946;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo></math>Neglected as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>&#946;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;is positive<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>&#946;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p>"
  }
}